*---------------------------------------------------------------
* errno.spawn.equ -- ERR_2BIG (argv too large for spawn()),
* docs/SYSCALL.md ruling on ABI FRICTION item 4 / docs/LIMITS.
* md. Split out of inc/errno.equ (task #8, docs/SELFHOST-
* CONVERSION.md phase 1) -- reference-set scan shows this is the
* ONLY errno.equ code any src/bin/*.s program (sh.s, for its own
* spawn() error handling) references directly; every other code
* is kernel-internal (inc/errno.krn.equ). Kept its own
* file rather than folded into errno.krn.equ so sh.s -- and
* the kernel's own spawn path (procspawn.s/procspawn2.s), which
* also produces this code -- never has to PUT the whole
* kernel-only error table for one code.
*
* `put`-only file (no code/org/dsk), same precondition
* discipline as memmap.equ -- the top-level file must `put`
* this directly.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

ERR_NOEXEC        equ   $EB   ;spawn named a file not
                              ;BIN ($06) or SYS ($FF): V7's
                              ;ENOEXEC. Executability is decided
                              ;by inspection at spawn, no exec
                              ;bit (docs/EXEC-SHEBANG.md)
ERR_2BIG          equ   $E7   ;argument list too long --
                              ;spawn()'s argv exceeded ARG_MAX
                              ;bytes of packed strings, or
                              ;ARGV_PTR_LIM bytes of pointer
                              ;array (inc/memmap.equ). The
                              ;E2BIG role docs/LIMITS.md asked
                              ;for: a too-large argv must FAIL,
                              ;because the alternative -- stage
                              ;what fits, drop the rest -- runs
                              ;a DIFFERENT command than the one
                              ;asked for and says nothing.
